<h1>least common multiple</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The least integer which is a multiple of given integers.  For instance, LCM(6, 10) = 30.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> LCM.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="greatestCommonDivisor.html"><em>greatest common divisor</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Flower Brackets <a href="https://www.flowerbrackets.com/java-program-find-gcd-lcm-two-numbers-euclids-algorithm/" target="_blank">(Java)</a>. 

